<title>TURKEY: Turkish Tupras H1 losses jump.</title>
<headline>Turkish Tupras H1 losses jump.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>January-June 1997 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>				    H1 1997	   H1 1996</p>
<p>				    -------	   -------</p>
<p>    Per share loss   (lira) 7,547.43  vs     834.99</p>
<p>    Loss			 35,231.61  vs   3,901.05</p>
<p>    Net sales		 251,838.33  vs 132,509.54</p>
<p>    Operating loss	   32,402.37  vs   7,720.70</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	1,848.38  vs   5,186.62</p>
<p>    Interest paid	     3,547.33  vs     581.10</p>
<p>    Total debts	     174,736.69  vs  88,927.55</p>
<p>    Equity		    (14,783.86) vs (18,994.46)</p>
<p>    Capital		     4,672.00  vs   4,672.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkish oil refinery Tupras-Turkiye Petrol Rafinerileri A.S. is slated for privatisation with 96.41 percent of its capital held by the privatisation administration OIB.</p>
<p>The company's first quarter loss was 26.88 trillion lira.</p>
<p>Tupras raised petroleum prices by seven to nine percent late on Sunday -- the second hike since the coalition government took office in late June.</p>
<p>It completed to issue 2.7 bonuses and 2.7 rights per 1,000 lira nominal-valued existing shares on August 12, to increase its capitaL to 29,900.8 billion lira from the current 4,672 billion.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 78 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in June.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212 275 08 75</p>
</text>
